  "id": "sound-pressure-level",
  "term": "sound-pressure level",
  "definition": "Sound-pressure level is a measure of how strong a sound is, expressed in decibels. In this context, it is used as an acoustic indicator to compare environmental noise, such as the louder sound from an aircraft flying lower overhead.",
